  "question": "Explain the difference between mass and weight.",
  "gold_answer": "# Introduction\n\n---\n\n## Definition\n\nMass and weight are distinct physical parameters that describe different structural qualities of matter.\n\nMass is a measure of the total quantity of matter contained within an object and reflects its inherent inertial resistance to acceleration.\n\nWeight is the gravitational force vector exerted on an object by a massive central body, such as the Earth.\n\n---\n\n## Comparison Matrix\n\n| Characteristics | Mass | Weight |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Quantity Type** | Scalar property (Magnitude only). | Vector property (Magnitude and direction). |\n| **Location Factor** | Invariant; remains identical across all locations in the universe. | Variable; changes depending on the local gravitational acceleration field. |\n| **Measurement Instrument** | Measured using a balance scale. | Measured using a calibrated spring scale. |\n| **SI System Unit** | Kilogram ($\\text{kg}$). | Newton ($\\text{N}$). |\n\n---\n\n## Real-world Example\n\nAn astronaut has a mass of $60 \\text{ kg}$ on Earth.\n* **On Earth's Surface:** Their mass is $60 \\text{ kg}$, and their weight force is approximately $$60 \\times 9.8 = 588 \\text{ N}$$.\n* **On Moon's Surface:** Their mass remains exactly $60 \\text{ kg}$, but their weight drops to one-sixth of its Earth value ($98 \\text{ N}$) because the Moon's local gravitational pull is weaker.\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nMass is an unchanging scalar property intrinsic to an object, whereas weight is a variable vector force that scales with the strength of the surrounding gravitational field.",
  "candidate_response": "<div style=\"font-family: 'Segoe UI', sans-serif; max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px; background: #f8f9fa; min-height: 100vh;\">\n\n<!-- PAGE TITLE -->\n<div style=\"margin-bottom: 28px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 13px; color: #6c757d; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; margin-bottom: 6px;\">Physics · Mechanics</div>\n  <h1 style=\"font-size: 32px; font-weight: 700; color: #1a1a2e; margin: 0 0 8px 0;\">Mass vs. Weight</h1>\n  <p style=\"font-size: 16px; color: #495057; margin: 0; line-height: 1.6;\">Two of the most commonly confused concepts in physics — here's exactly how they differ.</p>\n</div>\n\n---\n\n<!-- QUICK DEFINITION CARDS -->\n<div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; margin-bottom: 24px;\">\n\n  <div style=\"background: #ffffff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px; border-left: 4px solid #4361ee; box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.07);\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: #4361ee; margin-bottom: 8px;\">⚛️ Mass</div>\n    <div style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #1a1a2e; margin-bottom: 6px;\">The amount of matter in an object.</div>\n    <div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #6c757d; line-height: 1.6;\">It is an <strong>intrinsic property</strong> — it does not change regardless of location, gravity, or environment.</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #ffffff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px; border-left: 4px solid #f72585; box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.07);\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: #f72585; margin-bottom: 8px;\">🌍 Weight</div>\n    <div style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #1a1a2e; margin-bottom: 6px;\">The gravitational force acting on that mass.</div>\n    <div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #6c757d; line-height: 1.6;\">It is a <strong>force</strong> — it changes depending on the strength of gravity at your location.</div>\n  </div>\n\n</div>\n\n---\n\n<!-- FORMULA CARD -->\n<div style=\"background: #ffffff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 24px; margin-bottom: 24px; box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.07); border-top: 4px solid #4361ee;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: #4361ee; margin-bottom: 16px;\">📐 Core Formula</div>\n  <div style=\"background: #f0f4ff; border-radius: 10px; padding: 24px; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 16px;\">\n\n$$W = m \\times g$$\n\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr; gap: 12px; margin-top: 16px;\">\n    <div style=\"background: #f8f9fa; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px; text-align: center;\">\n      <div style=\"font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700; color: #f72585;\">W</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 12px; color: #6c757d; margin-top: 4px;\">Weight</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 11px; color: #adb5bd;\">Newtons (N)</div>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"background: #f8f9fa; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px; text-align: center;\">\n      <div style=\"font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700; color: #4361ee;\">m</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 12px; color: #6c757d; margin-top: 4px;\">Mass</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 11px; color: #adb5bd;\">Kilograms (kg)</div>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"background: #f8f9fa; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px; text-align: center;\">\n      <div style=\"font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700; color: #06d6a0;\">g</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 12px; color: #6c757d; margin-top: 4px;\">Gravitational Acceleration</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 11px; color: #adb5bd;\">9.8 m/s² on Earth</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n---\n\n<!-- KEY CHARACTERISTICS TABLE -->\n<div style=\"background: #ffffff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 24px; margin-bottom: 24px; box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.07);\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: #4361ee; margin-bottom: 16px;\">📊 Side-by-Side Comparison</div>\n  <div style=\"overflow-x: auto;\">\n    <table style=\"width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 14px;\">\n      <thead>\n        <tr style=\"background: #f0f4ff;\">\n          <th style=\"padding: 12px 16px; text-align: left; color: #495057; font-weight: 600; border-bottom: 2px solid #dee2e6;\">Property</th>\n          <th style=\"padding: 12px 16px; text-align: left; color: #4361ee; font-weight: 600; border-bottom: 2px solid #dee2e6;\">⚛️ Mass</th>\n          <th style=\"padding: 12px 16px; text-align: left; color: #f72585; font-weight: 600; border-bottom: 2px solid #dee2e6;\">🌍 Weight</th>\n        </tr>\n      </thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid #f1f3f5;\">\n          <td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; color: #6c757d; font-weight: 500;\">Type</td>\n          <td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; color: #1a1a2e;\">Scalar quantity</td>\n          <td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; color: #1a1a2e;\">Vector quantity</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr style=\"background: #fafafa; border-bottom: 1px solid #f1f3f5;\">\n          <td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; color: #6c757d; font-weight: 500;\">SI Unit</td>\n          <td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; color: #1a1a2e;\">Kilogram (kg)</td>\n          <td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; color: #1a1a2e;\">Newton (N)</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid #f1f3f5;\">\n          <td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; color: #6c757d; font-weight: 500;\">Changes with gravity?</td>\n          <td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; color: #06d6a0; font-weight: 600;\">✗ Never</td>\n          <td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; color: #f72585; font-weight: 600;\">✓ Always</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr style=\"background: #fafafa; border-bottom: 1px solid #f1f3f5;\">\n          <td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; color: #6c757d; font-weight: 500;\">Measured with</td>\n          <td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; color: #1a1a2e;\">Balance scale</td>\n          <td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; color: #1a1a2e;\">Spring scale</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; color: #6c757d; font-weight: 500;\">In deep space (no gravity)</td>\n          <td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; color: #1a1a2e;\">Stays the same</td>\n          <td style=\"padding: 12px 16px; color: #1a1a2e;\">Becomes zero</td>\n        </tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n---\n\n<!-- REAL WORLD EXAMPLE -->\n<div style=\"background: #ffffff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 24px; margin-bottom: 24px; box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.07);\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: #06d6a0; margin-bottom: 16px;\">🚀 Real-World Example — Astronaut on the Moon</div>\n\n  <div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px;\">\n\n    <div style=\"background: #f0fff8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px; border: 1px solid #b7f5d8;\">\n      <div style=\"font-weight: 700; color: #1a1a2e; margin-bottom: 8px;\">⚛️ Mass stays constant</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #495057; line-height: 1.6;\">An astronaut with a mass of <strong>70 kg</strong> on Earth still has a mass of <strong>70 kg</strong> on the Moon. Mass never changes.</div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div style=\"background: #fff0f6; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px; border: 1px solid #ffb3d1;\">\n      <div style=\"font-weight: 700; color: #1a1a2e; margin-bottom: 8px;\">🌍 Weight changes</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #495057; line-height: 1.6;\">\n        On Earth: <strong>70 × 9.8 = 686 N</strong><br/>\n        On Moon: <strong>70 × 1.6 = 112 N</strong><br/>\n        <span style=\"color: #f72585;\">That's about ⅙ of their Earth weight!</span>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n---\n\n<!-- IMPORTANT NOTE -->\n<div style=\"background: #fffbea; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px; margin-bottom: 24px; border-left: 4px solid #ffd60a; box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: #e9c46a; margin-bottom: 8px;\">⚠️ Common Misconception</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #495057; line-height: 1.7;\">\n    In everyday language, people say <em>\"I weigh 70 kg\"</em> — but scientifically, that is your <strong>mass</strong>. Your <strong>weight</strong> would be expressed in Newtons. The confusion exists because on Earth's surface, gravity is roughly constant, so the two are often used interchangeably in daily life.\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n---\n\n<!-- SUMMARY -->\n<div style=\"background: #1a1a2e; border-radius: 12px; padding: 24px; margin-bottom: 8px; color: white;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: #a0aec0; margin-bottom: 16px;\">🎯 Summary</div>\n  <div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px;\">\n    <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;\">\n      <div style=\"background: #4361ee; border-radius: 50%; width: 8px; height: 8px; margin-top: 6px; flex-shrink: 0;\"></div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: #e2e8f0;\">Mass is <strong style=\"color: white;\">what you're made of</strong> — measured in kg, never changes.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;\">\n      <div style=\"background: #f72585; border-radius: 50%; width: 8px; height: 8px; margin-top: 6px; flex-shrink: 0;\"></div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: #e2e8f0;\">Weight is <strong style=\"color: white;\">the force gravity exerts</strong> on that mass — measured in N, varies by location.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;\">\n      <div style=\"background: #06d6a0; border-radius: 50%; width: 8px; height: 8px; margin-top: 6px; flex-shrink: 0;\"></div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: #e2e8f0;\">The relationship is <strong style=\"color: white;\">W = mg</strong>, where g = 9.8 m/s² on Earth.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;\">\n      <div style=\"background: #ffd60a; border-radius: 50%; width: 8px; height: 8px; margin-top: 6px; flex-shrink: 0;\"></div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: #e2e8f0;\">Weight is a <strong style=\"color: white;\">vector</strong> (has direction); mass is a <strong style=\"color: white;\">scalar</strong> (no direction).</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n</div>",
